  "steps": [
    "Boil 100g raw soya chunks with 1 tsp salt for 5 minutes. Drain, let them cool slightly, then squeeze out the water.",
    "To a pan on medium heat, add: 1 tbsp ghee, ¼ tsp turmeric, 1 tsp chilli powder, 1 tsp coriander powder, 1 tsp ginger-garlic paste.",
    "Mix well, then add the boiled soya chunks and sauté for about 3 minutes.",
    "Now add 1 sliced onion, 1 sliced green chilli, a handful of freshly chopped coriander.",
    "Mix everything well and set aside.",
    "In a separate bowl, add 250g high-protein Greek yogurt, ½ tsp salt, 3 finely chopped garlic cloves.",
    "Mix until well combined.",
    "For the tadka heat 3 tbsp mustard oil in a small pan until it just starts to smoke, then switch off the heat.",
    "Add ¼ tsp turmeric, 1 tsp red chilli powder, 1 tsp kasuri methi.",
    "Pour the hot tadka into the yogurt and mix well.",
    "Finally, pour the yogurt mixture over the soya chunks, mix everything together, and your Soya Chukani is ready to serve!"
  ],
